documentation
project

	^ 'HSK is a Chinese learning toolkit for Pharo. It models Chinese characters and words (traditional and simplified forms, pinyin, zhuyin, definitions, radicals, phonems, frequency, HSK module, related words), keeps a CC-CEDICT-derived dictionary in a character trie, embeds an HSK 1-6 character corpus and a CEDICT snapshot, and adds spaced-repetition learning (SRS). On top of the SRS model there is a desktop application built with Toplo on Bloc (see HSKDesktopShell): user sessions with SRS goals, a knowledge evolution overview, pinyin exercises (Reminder and Quiz), user selection/creation and a writing style preference (traditional/simplified). The code is the package HSK of the Iceberg repository ChineseCharacters. Environment: Pharo 14.0.0 (update 140790). Libraries: Pharo standard library, Zinc for HTTP crawling, Bloc and Toplo (full stack loaded) for the app; the widget reuse priority is Toplo, then Bloc, then Pharo standard.'